                <pb facs="0754" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/8641: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Beaulac</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-18T19:00:00-05:00">January 18, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Your despatch no. 2715, January 15. The Department perceives no objection
                    whatever to your making clear its position, as expressed in the Department’s
                    telegram no. 3, January 13, 5 p.m., to anyone in your discretion, and
                    specifically to the persons mentioned in your despatch under reference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
